### AI support assistant — demo requests
### Run the AppHost first. Open this file in VS Code (REST Client extension) or Visual Studio
### and click "Send Request" above each request.

@Catalog = https://localhost:7234
@Bff = https://localhost:7176

### 1. Simple Q&A (GET) straight to Catalog
GET {{Catalog}}/products/ai/support?question=What can I use to cook food while camping?
Accept: application/json

### 2. Budget question — the answer should use real names and prices
GET {{Catalog}}/products/ai/support?question=I have 50 dollars. What can I buy for a night in the forest?
Accept: application/json

### 3. Grounding test — we do not sell this, so the assistant should say it doesn't know
GET {{Catalog}}/products/ai/support?question=Do you sell mountain bikes?
Accept: application/json

### 4. Off-topic test — the assistant should politely refuse
GET {{Catalog}}/products/ai/support?question=Who won the cricket world cup?
Accept: application/json

### 5. Chat with history (POST) — follow-up question "is it waterproof?" refers to the jacket
POST {{Catalog}}/products/ai/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Is it good for rain?",
  "history": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "I need something to wear on a hike." },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "The Outdoor Rain Jacket ($49.99) will keep you warm and dry in all weathers." }
  ]
}

### 6. Same Q&A through the BFF (the way the React frontend calls it)
GET {{Bff}}/api/products/ai/support?question=Which product helps me see at night?
Accept: application/json

### 7. Chat through the BFF — POST needs the X-CSRF header
POST {{Bff}}/api/products/ai/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF: 1

{
  "question": "Suggest a full camping kit under 200 dollars."
}

### 8. Validation — empty question returns 400
GET {{Catalog}}/products/ai/support?question=
Accept: application/json
